1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,657
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:13,100
Believe in what I do.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,937
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't wanna live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,777
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,540
We believe in one another.

26
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:00,420
What a nice breeze!

27
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:12,437
Nami, if you don't mind, I'd
like to stop the ship here.

28
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:15,480
It'll just be for a
moment. Stop? What for?

29
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:18,232
I have a very important mission for Karoo.

30
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:19,570
Karoo?

31
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:31,440
Karoo, I need you to go to Alubarna Palace
and deliver this letter to my father.

32
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:35,000
It contains everything
uncovered by Igaran and myself.

33
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:38,957
The details of Crocodile's nefarious
plans for this country are in here.

34
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:39,870
Also,

35
00:02:39,953 --> 00:02:43,557
it lets him know that I've returned
to Alabasta safe and sound and

36
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:46,777
in the company of brave friends
willing to help us in our struggle.

37
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:49,740
Well, then, can you do this for me, Kaido?

38
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:56,660
Now, be careful to
conserve your water, okay?

39
00:02:58,440 --> 00:02:59,270
Good luck!

40
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:00,617
You can do it, Duck!

41
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,347
Go let my father know, Kaido.

42
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,735
There's hope for this kingdom at last.

43
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,440
I said conserve, not consume!

44
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,400
Thank you, and good luck.

45
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:23,100
Well, I did know the crocodile
was here in Alabasta.

46
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,500
But him trying to steal a kingdom?

47
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:30,177
That sounds like a bad
joke Because why would a

48
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:33,017
pirate drop anchor in
one spot and settle down?

49
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:36,977
Crocodile trying to usurp the throne
of Alabasta doesn't make sense Alright,

50
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,920
let's set this out! Hold on!

51
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:43,329
You know, there could be another
side to this takeover thing

52
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:44,950
Huh?

53
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,800
Like some sort of deeper
goal or something.

54
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,320
We're finally here!

55
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,417
Wow, so we're going into the desert?

56
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,457
Does anyone know how hot
it's supposed to get?

57
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,257
Over 100 degrees in the daytime.

58
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,170
What?

59
00:03:57,253 --> 00:03:58,457
Please tell me you're joking!

60
00:03:58,540 --> 00:03:59,960
Ah, Nami, what happened?

61
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,777
Where's your dancer outfit?

62
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:02,940
Ah, you too!

63
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,184
Vivi, why are you wearing that?

64
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:08,100
Because any exposed
skin will get sunburned.

65
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,557
You have to cover up in the desert.

66
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:13,640
But those outfits are so sexy.

67
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,080
Put these on, Luffy. Oh, thank you.

68
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,260
Time to drop anchor. Right.

69
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,280
Yuba, here we come!

70
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:34,440
What are those?

71
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:42,850
Turtles?

72
00:04:42,933 --> 00:04:44,269
No, I think they're seals.

73
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:45,460
Kong Fu Da Gongs!

74
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,297
If you want to come insure,
you'll have to beat me first,

75
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:51,777
but I doubt that'll happen,
you bunch of cowards.

76
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:52,690
He says.

77
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,317
Nobody calls me a coward
and gets away with it.

78
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,440
Here comes the pain! No, wait!

79
00:05:01,980 --> 00:05:04,100
Kong Fu Da Gongs are really strong!

80
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,297
See, they're not too tough!

81
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:09,640
That's bad, too!

82
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:14,680
What the?

83
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,420
It's one of their rules.

84
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:20,917
If they lose a Kong fu match,
they become the winner's pupil.

85
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,040
You don't say.

86
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:27,540
They think you're their master now! Right!

87
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,980
Everyone after me! Now punch!

88
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:32,360
Now, like this!

89
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,150
Yeah!

90
00:05:34,233 --> 00:05:35,080
Now harder!

91
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,540
And now, lift!

92
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:40,040
Let's go! Right!

93
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:41,790
Yeah!

94
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:49,900
Hope all you guys enjoy the food! See ya!

95
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,780
All you guys. Food.

96
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:54,037
Now do you get it?

97
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:57,277
No, they said they wanted to go with
us, so why couldn't we let them?

98
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:00,657
We don't have the food and water
to take care of a group that big.

99
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:01,570
Moron.

100
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,630
Honestly,

101
00:06:02,713 --> 00:06:05,197
I don't know what we would have done if
Chopper hadn't persuaded them to stay.

102
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:06,110
Yeah!

103
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,977
They kept saying, where you
go, we'll follow, Master.

104
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:11,597
They really would have, too, if
I hadn't given them that food.

105
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:14,257
And now our food supply's
gotten a lot smaller.

106
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:15,170
Thanks, Luffy.

107
00:06:15,253 --> 00:06:16,083
Thanks.

108
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,280
He's a handful.

109
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,559
You're telling me.

110
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:30,770
What's this?

111
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,440
Are we in Yuba already?

112
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,030
No.

113
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,470
Wow.

114
00:06:35,553 --> 00:06:36,383
This is Aramalu.

115
00:06:36,466 --> 00:06:39,085
It was known far and wide
as the City of Green.

116
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,460
It was green?

117
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:43,777
Take a good look around, everyone.

118
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:47,160
This is what Baroque Works
has been doing to my country.

119
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:51,246
The people of Alabasta, this is
what they've had to go through.

120
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:56,360
Wow, there's nothing
here at all anymore, huh?

121
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:00,080
No, it's nothing but a ghost town now.

122
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:04,677
But up until a few short years ago, it
was a thriving city full of gardens,

123
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,525
palm trees, and lush greenery.

124
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:07,870
This place?

125
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:11,240
Rain was always scarce here.

126
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:14,897
But by saving every last drop
of water and using it wisely,

127
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:17,745
the city was able to make
the foliage flourish.

128
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:20,686
Unfortunately, that
stopped when the rain did.

129
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:22,797
Not a single drop of water has fallen in

130
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:25,527
any part of this country
for three years now.

131
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:26,590
Three years?

132
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:28,640
Wow, that long? But wait.

133
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:32,417
Even without rain, there was still
the river as another water source.

134
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,330
And it's close.

135
00:07:33,413 --> 00:07:35,797
Why couldn't they just pipe
the water in from over there?

136
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:38,351
Well, the answer to that is just up ahead.

137
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,457
Even though it's a desert kingdom,

138
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:46,697
never in the thousands
of years of Alabasta's

139
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,177
history has the rain
ever stopped completely.

140
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,090
However,

141
00:07:50,173 --> 00:07:53,037
there was one place in the country
where the rain fell more than usual,

142
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:54,179
much more in fact.

143
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:59,461
Alubarna, the capital, the city
where the king's palace is located.

144
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:22,419
The people of the land
called it the king's miracle.

145
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:25,429
At least they did until
one particular day.

146
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,200
Get that cargo unloaded!

147
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,066
We've got a schedule to keep!

148
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:39,020
We're losing it! What happened?

149
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,010
What happened?

150
00:08:42,093 --> 00:08:43,314
Is everyone all right?

151
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:44,750
Damn it!

152
00:08:44,833 --> 00:08:46,257
What are we supposed to do now?

153
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:48,046
It's a delivery for the king!

154
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:50,297
What's he gonna do when
it doesn't arrive on time?

155
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,145
Is green powders for the king?

156
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:53,090
What is it?

157
00:08:53,173 --> 00:08:54,003
What is it?

158
00:08:54,086 --> 00:08:55,457
How the hell should we know?

159
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:57,737
We're only following your king's orders.

160
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:59,060
We're just couriers.

161
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:00,850
Run!

162
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:05,660
Wait a minute.

163
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,160
Could this be?

164
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:08,640
Dance powder?

165
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:13,140
Oh, so you've heard of it? Yes.

166
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:14,740
I sure have.

167
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:15,940
It summons rain.

168
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,560
A powdered can?

169
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:20,397
I've only heard stories
about it, But apparently,

170
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:24,297
dance powder was created by a researcher
in a country where it never rained.

171
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:27,851
Burning it creates a misty
smoke, which rises into the sky.

172
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:30,577
Once it reaches the clouds,
it causes them to rain.

173
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:34,425
In essence, it gives you the
ability to create rain on the spot.

174
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:37,620
So, in fact, as its name suggests,

175
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:41,177
the country that developed dance
powder was happy enough to dance.

176
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:42,580
It got lots of rain.

177
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:43,897
But there is a catch.

178
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:46,215
Its neighboring country had a drought.

179
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:48,760
Let me explain how it works. Now,

180
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:51,857
the mist from the burned
dance powder targets

181
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:54,197
small clouds that aren't
ready to rain yet.

182
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:57,177
It artificially matures
them into full rain clouds.

183
00:09:57,260 --> 00:10:00,057
Those clouds would have
naturally grown into rain clouds,

184
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:02,057
but when they were further downwind.

185
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:03,100
Oh, I get it.

186
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:06,417
It steals all the rain that would have
normally gone to a neighboring country.

187
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:08,377
That must have caused some big problems.

188
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,400
Oh, it did.

189
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:11,857
A war broke out between the two countries.

190
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:13,200
Ever since then,

191
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:16,177
the world government has
instituted a worldwide ban

192
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:19,017
on the production and
possession of dance powder.

193
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:22,000
Even so, some of it managed
to show up here, huh?

194
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:26,820
When it happened, the country had
been experiencing strange weather.

195
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,353
There had been no rain.

196
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:33,565
Not a single drop had fallen anywhere
except one place, and that was the capital.

197
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,471
No wonder we haven't had any rain in ages!

198
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:39,297
The kings stole it from the
capital using this dance powder!

199
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:42,792
So Alibana's reign wasn't a
miracle at all, it was a sham!

200
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,706
Yeah, one that's left
us parched and starving.

201
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,664
This is all King Cobra's fault.

202
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:49,450
Vivi!

203
00:10:49,533 --> 00:10:51,860
That means your dad is
the bad guy here! No!

204
00:10:52,180 --> 00:10:53,651
You idiot, he was framed!

205
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:59,405
Her sweet, dear old dad would
never do such a thing, you got it!

206
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:05,634
Of course, my father didn't have
anything to do with it, he was innocent.

207
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,590
Unfortunately,

208
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:12,557
a large amount of dance powder was discovered
inside his palace shortly thereafter.

209
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:13,470
Huh.

210
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:16,365
They even had people
working inside the palace.

211
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:20,380
So, what is this? A road?

212
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:25,460
No, it used to be a large canal that piped
in fresh water from the Sandora River.

213
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:26,530
Huh?

214
00:11:26,613 --> 00:11:27,877
Until someone destroyed it.

215
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,537
Now do you see what happened?

216
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:30,977
With its canal gone,

217
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:34,825
the city of Green lost its only
remaining source of fresh water.

218
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:40,240
The people here waited and prayed,
but sadly, rain never came.

219
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,230
Wow,

220
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:45,357
something like that and
the dance powder incident

221
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:48,057
would really make people
distrust their king.

222
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,940
That's exactly what
Crocodile planned, I bet.

223
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:54,780
With no more water, fighting
began to break out in Aramaloo.

224
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,757
To escape the violence here,

225
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:59,737
there was only one thing the
exhausted citizens could do.

226
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:03,920
They abandoned the city and left
for other oases in search of water.

227
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:11,580
And then, the city of Green withered away.

228
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:16,777
Someone's collapsed!

229
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:20,272
Wait, you mean there are still
people living in this city?

230
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:34,800
What did my father and all of the other
good people, what did they ever do?

231
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,920
We don't deserve this.

232
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:40,397
It's hard enough to live in the desert.

233
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:42,737
Every day it's a struggle just to survive.

234
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:46,977
Somehow the people of Alabasta found a
way to do it and they led happy lives.

235
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:49,320
But Crocodile destroyed those lives.

236
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,457
What gives him the right to do that?

237
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:52,370
What?

238
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:53,720
All the while,

239
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:57,837
as one of the seven warlords, he passes
himself off as a hero of the people.

240
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,597
They don't know what he's really doing.

241
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:01,797
No one realizes that
he's actually deceiving

242
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:04,527
the entire country even
as they cheer him on.

243
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:09,600
Crocodile! Crocodile!
Crocodile! Crocodile!

244
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,160
I can't!

245
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:14,000
I can't let him get away with this!

246
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:23,820
Oh well.

247
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,261
I hope that made him feel better.

248
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:40,490
V .V.

249
00:13:40,573 --> 00:13:41,457
Let's get moving, Kay.

250
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:42,893
I'm itching to do this.

251
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:46,010
He's right.

252
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:47,179
Let's get to Yuba.

253
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:50,868
That's where the Rebel
Army is, right, Yuba?

254
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:53,531
Yes, I have to stop them.

255
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:55,677
I'm going to persuade their leader.

256
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:56,590
How so?

257
00:13:56,860 --> 00:14:00,737
I'll tell the Rebel leader the truth,
that all of this is Crocodiles doing.

258
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:03,761
And have him stop all of
this pointless bloodshed.

259
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,330
Let's go.

260
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:29,480
I'm burning up.

261
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,980
I don't think I can even sweat anymore.

262
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:35,377
Will you please spare us
the melodramatics, Luffy?

263
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:37,737
You're only going to wear yourself out.

264
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:39,702
Gee, I guess he's not listening.

265
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:43,800
I can't go on.

266
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,920
I can't take hot weather.

267
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:48,080
I'm fighting cold weather.

268
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:50,837
It's because of all that fur.

269
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:53,979
Why don't you take off that
stupid reindeer costume?

270
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:57,260
What did you just say to me? Red nose!

271
00:14:57,900 --> 00:15:00,100
Don't make fun of reindeer! MONSTER!

272
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:05,357
Chopper, don't turn yourself big
or I'm going to quit pulling you.

273
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,877
Who are you calling a
monster, you bird-nosed freak?

274
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:10,677
You better take it easy on the
nose or I'll have to get topped.

275
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,080
Turn small, will ya?

276
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:20,154
Hey, the desert doesn't seem
to bother you much, Phoebe.

277
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,337
Well, I was born and
raised in this country,

278
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:24,773
so I guess you could say I'm used to it.

279
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:28,900
So, what's with all these hills?

280
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,920
I was expecting a desert to be more flat!

281
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:35,000
This is a very old desert.

282
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:39,160
Some of the sand dunes here are
over 900 feet high. 900 feet?

283
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,700
Oh my god, no!

284
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:42,430
That's...

285
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:44,260
That's a mountain!

286
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,740
No hot water!

287
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:48,760
Just one drink, Luffy.

288
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,240
Just one mouthful.

289
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:54,400
Don't drink so much! Idiot!

290
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:56,697
You'd better save some
of that water for Usa!

291
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:58,956
Hold on, you just had some odd kicks!

292
00:15:59,080 --> 00:15:59,910
Give me that kick!

293
00:15:59,993 --> 00:16:00,823
Stop it, you guys!

294
00:16:00,906 --> 00:16:03,257
You're only going to wear
yourselves out if you keep it up!

295
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:04,516
Hey, she started it!

296
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:06,140
It's your fault!

297
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:08,280
It's always his fault!

298
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:14,500
Hey, Sanji, let's have one of
those box lunches. Not yet.

299
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,520
Not until Vivi says so.

300
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:18,897
Come on, Vivi, how about it?

301
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:19,810
Let's eat!

302
00:16:19,893 --> 00:16:20,723
Doesn't that sound good?

303
00:16:20,806 --> 00:16:23,097
But we're not even a
tenth of the way to Yuba,

304
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:25,917
Luffy, and we have to make our
supplies last the whole way.

305
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,300
Don't be silly, Vivi.

306
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,257
Haven't you heard the old proverb?

307
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:31,437
Make sure you eat whenever you're hungry.

308
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:34,037
Oh, quit making things
up, you big fat liar.

309
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:36,017
Okay, if you're that
hungry, I'll tell you what.

310
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,637
Why don't we stop and eat at the
next group of rocks we come to?

311
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,140
All right, rocks it is.

312
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,437
Onward to the next group of rocks.

313
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:46,157
Okay, guys, whoever wins at rock, paper,
scissors has to carry everybody's stuff.

314
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:47,475
Quit deciding things.

315
00:16:47,620 --> 00:16:51,280
And ready, go. No! Rock! Paper! Wait!

316
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:52,997
No, just hold on!

317
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,374
Hey, you started late!

318
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:56,740
I win! Idiot.

319
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,210
Heavy.

320
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:02,380
So heavy.

321
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:08,297
Why am I doing all the work?

322
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:10,097
You said the winner carries all.

323
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:11,157
Now shut up and haul!

324
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,240
Make sure you don't drop anything!

325
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:19,640
Hey, guys!

326
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,409
I spotted Rockstead ahead!

327
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:22,620
You mean it!

328
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:24,240
It's lunchtime!

329
00:17:25,740 --> 00:17:26,570
Whoo!

330
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:27,660
That's so fast!

331
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,320
Oh, shade.

332
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:36,140
It feels so good.

333
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:56,260
I need help!

334
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:58,950
That's weird.

335
00:17:59,033 --> 00:17:59,863
Why is he coming back?

336
00:17:59,946 --> 00:18:02,477
There's a whole flock of injured
birds here that can't move!

337
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:04,260
We need a doctor! Chomper!

338
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:08,380
All right, let's go, Chomper! Coming!

339
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:13,160
We gotta help those birds! What
birds? Wait a minute, Luffy!

340
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:16,182
Those birds might not be
what you think they are!

341
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:17,390
Huh?

342
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,620
All of our stuff is gone.

343
00:18:21,860 --> 00:18:23,080
We've been had.

344
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:25,960
But I saw them!

345
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:29,297
There was a whole flock of
dying birds lying right there!

346
00:18:29,380 --> 00:18:30,480
I'm so sorry.

347
00:18:30,740 --> 00:18:32,916
I should have mentioned this earlier.

348
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:35,877
What do soggy birds
are desert bandits that

349
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:38,397
deceive travelers and
steal their belongings?

350
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,080
You gotta be kidding!

351
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,304
You mean these birds play dead?

352
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,660
What a lousy bunch of crooks!

353
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,415
This is all my fault.

354
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:48,913
Those birds tricked me!

355
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:52,257
Luffy, you dolt, is that all
you have to say for yourself?

356
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:53,437
There were three days'

357
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:54,857
worth of supplies in those packs,

358
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:56,737
and you just had to go
and let a bunch of stupid

359
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:59,177
birds rob us blind in
the middle of a desert.

360
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:02,777
How are we supposed to get across
this wasteland without food or water?

361
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:04,742
I hope you're proud of yourself.

362
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,617
Come on, it's not my fault.

363
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:08,237
I mean, they outsmarted me.

364
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:10,379
You mean you're dumber than a bird?

365
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:11,710
What's that?

366
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,334
Knock it off, you two.

367
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:14,957
No, you're not that smart!

368
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:16,360
Just save your energy.

369
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:20,448
At times like this, it's better
just to let them have it out.

370
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:21,370
You're such a moron!

371
00:19:21,453 --> 00:19:22,283
You are for what am I?

372
00:19:22,366 --> 00:19:23,196
Fine with me.

373
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,457
Let's just take a break.

374
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:28,893
This heat is just starting to
wear on everybody's nerves.

375
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,337
I'm sure we'll manage food and water wise.

376
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,177
It's nothing that'll kill us right away.

377
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:35,257
Let's put it out of our minds for now.

378
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:39,869
Yeah, that's a good idea because when
I think about it, I get really thirsty.

379
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:45,870
Ah!

380
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:50,590
Ah!

381
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:52,930
Ah!

382
00:19:53,013 --> 00:19:54,382
Gennosaurus, jump back in there!

383
00:19:55,020 --> 00:19:55,850
Ah!

384
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:57,280
No, Luffy!

385
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:58,480
Don't chase them!

386
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,540
That idiot. Wait!

387
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,617
Will you be able to find your way back?

388
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:05,180
Get back here, you dope! Luffy!

389
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:09,470
Stop!

390
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:11,520
You can't get away from me!

391
00:20:16,740 --> 00:20:18,120
Get back here!

392
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,180
Come on, Luffy.

393
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,300
Hurry it up.

394
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:28,960
Um, you don't suppose he
could be lost, do you?

395
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:34,121
There are still so many desert dangers I
haven't had a chance to warn him about yet.

396
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:36,870
What's that?

397
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,924
What on earth is that rumbling?

398
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:54,080
Is it another sandstorm?

399
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,800
No, wait, that looks like...

400
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:01,500
It's Luffy!

401
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:04,220
Oh no, it can't be.

402
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:06,170
Huh?

403
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:08,720
Why is he on a camel?

404
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:14,197
Someone want to tell me
what the hell's chasing him?

405
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,560
I can't really tell,

406
00:21:15,740 --> 00:21:19,740
but it looks like there's something
in the sand burrowing after him.

407
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:25,500
What is that?

408
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:28,300
It's a Sandora Dragon! It's a what?

409
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:29,660
A Sandora Dragon!

410
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:32,217
They're the biggest reptile
that lives in the desert.

411
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:35,077
They wait under the sand for
their prey and then ambush them.

412
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:38,657
They have razor-sharp fangs and
claws, but they hardly ever use them.

413
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:40,597
Because they're so incredibly huge,

414
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:43,217
they usually just end up
swallowing their victims whole!

415
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:46,237
I gotta admit that boy
does have a talent for

416
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:48,777
attracting trouble
right and all of us have

417
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:51,337
the scars to prove it
What kind of crap star

418
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:54,185
was he born under to
attract trouble like that?

419
00:22:17,260 --> 00:22:18,997
You didn't have to go that far.

420
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:23,433
Whenever those guys fight, it almost
makes me feel sorry for the monsters.

421
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:31,357
Is this convenient?

422
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:34,205
These rocks are just like
a natural frying pan.

423
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:40,140
So, now that we have a moment, what's
the deal with the camel? I don't know.

424
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:44,077
It was getting eaten by the mystery
plants while I was chasing those birds.

425
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:45,937
It's obviously not a wild camel.

426
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:48,200
No, not with a saddle and bridle.

427
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,297
He's a passenger-carrying camel.

428
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:54,437
That's sure going to
make things a lot easier.

429
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:56,277
Yeah, that ought to be a real help.

430
00:22:56,360 --> 00:22:58,037
It looks like he could carry two.

431
00:22:58,120 --> 00:23:00,414
Camels do go hand-in-hand with deserts.

432
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:02,581
Great, I'll take the first shift.

433
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:05,110
Ow!

434
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:08,977
I'm a freedom-loving, hard-boiled,
yet compassionate son of the desert.

435
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:11,917
I'm very grateful to you for having
helped me out of that jam back there?

436
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,797
And I'll be glad to
give some of you a ride,

437
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:16,586
but I'm afraid I don't
accept male passengers.

438
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:20,820
I'm too macho.

439
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:29,408
I'm so sorry that my crewmates
are a bunch of ill-bred louts.

440
00:23:29,520 --> 00:23:32,697
Now, what should we call you, you
great big precious gamble, you?

441
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:34,360
Idiot! Moron! Doofus!

442
00:23:35,340 --> 00:23:36,516
Eyelash it is, then.

443
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:38,326
Uh, how'd you arrive at that?

444
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:40,860
Okay, climb on, Vivi.

445
00:23:41,300 --> 00:23:43,800
No, I'm fine. I can still walk. Thanks.

446
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:46,580
Just get on. Pervert camel.

447
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:48,080
Pervert camel.

448
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:49,560
Pervert camel.

449
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:51,500
This is great.

450
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:53,237
We should be able to make better time now.

451
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:58,217
We need to get to Yuba as fast as we can
so we'll be able to talk to the Rebel Army.

452
00:23:58,300 --> 00:23:59,460
Giddy up, Eyelash.

453
00:24:00,820 --> 00:24:02,180
Hey, wait for us.

454
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:03,517
Hurry up, guys.

455
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:06,777
If you get separated, you'll
never leave the desert alive.

456
00:24:06,860 --> 00:24:07,697
Well, thanks a lot.

457
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:09,477
I like this side of Nami, too.

458
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:10,437
What else is new?

459
00:24:10,520 --> 00:24:12,600
After them, hurry! Chopper, hop on!

460
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:14,540
Wait for us!
